-- title:
--   Vanishing of H¹ when all multiplicative 1-cocycles are coboundaries
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group and $V$ a commutative group, written multiplicatively, equipped with a multiplicative distributive action of $G$, i.e. $G$ acts on $V$ by group automorphisms ($g \cdot (xy) = (g\cdot x)(g\cdot y)$ and $g \cdot 1 = 1$). Assume that every function $f : G \to V$ satisfying the multiplicative $1$-cocycle condition in Mathlib's normalisation, $f(gh) = (g \cdot f(h))\, f(g)$ for all $g,h \in G$, is a multiplicative $1$-coboundary, that is, there is $x \in V$ with $f(g) = (g \cdot x)\,x^{-1}$ for all $g \in G$. The conclusion is that the first group cohomology of the $G$-representation `Rep.ofMulDistribMulAction G V`, whose underlying module is $V$ with its group law written additively and the given $G$-action, is a subsingleton: any two classes in $H^1$ coincide. Since $H^1$ carries a group structure, this is the statement $H^1(G,V) = 0$, expressed as a `Subsingleton` assertion rather than as an equality of objects. The groups $G$ and $V$ are taken in `Type`.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the elementwise multiplicative formulation of $1$-cocycles and $1$-coboundaries and the vanishing of Mathlib's $H^1$ of the associated representation, for a group acting by automorphisms on an abelian group written multiplicatively. It is used where vanishing of a degree-one cohomology group of a unit group or group of roots of unity is needed, for instance in the local-level arguments and in the construction of elements of prescribed norm in fields generated by $p$-adic roots of unity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_groupCohomology_subsingleton_H1_ofMulDistribMulAction.lean

import Mathlib

